findings.citation_text:
6-501.111 Roach activity was observed in the kitchen at the cook line, in the dish area, and at the server runway. Live roaches were observed in the following locations:
1. adult roach crawled out from under the reach-in cooler at the end of the cook line (across from dish area) - roach was immediately killed by the owner; 
2. adult roach in the corner by the soda syrup boxes; 
3. adult roach crawling from the floor and onto a box in the server area; 
4. juvenile roach on the floor under the dish machine; and
5. adult female (appeared to be dead) with an egg case (possibly viable?) on the floor at the far left wall of the dish area.
 Owner is currently working with pest control company to address the issue (see general comments for details).   
The premises shall be maintained free of pests. The presence of insects, rodents, and other pests shall be controlled to eliminate their presence by routinely inspecting incoming shipments of food and supplies; routinely inspecting the premises for evidence of pests; using methods, if pests are found, such as trapping devices or other means of pest control as specified under §§ 7-202.12, 7-206.12, and 7-206.13; and eliminating harborage conditions.

findings.comment:
750-800e Observed the following non-food contact surfaces to be soiled: 1) inside of the glass door Pepsi cooler (spill and food debris in base, door has grease smudges);
2) clean the reach-in freezer holding dressings (mold and food splash - a thermometer was discarded due to mold);
3) reach-in freezer holding plates (food debris);
4) BAR - a. speed rails (sticky/debris buildup), b. storage bin to left of 3 part sink (debris/splash), c. inside cabinets beneath draft beer lines (splash/debris), d. edges of beer cooler door seals (debris),   & e. 2 door cooler - bottom inside (sticky buildup) & shelving (black buildup);
5) ALCOHOL WALKIN - shelving (mold/buildup);
6) DRY STORAGE - shelving (powder buildup on lower shelves);   and
7) BACK PREP - a. kettle cooker by back 3 part sink (splash/food debris on general surfaces), b. lower shelves of prep tables (food debris/splash),  & c. under slicer (dust/food debris).

Non-food contact surfaces of equipment shall be cleaned as often as is necessary to keep the equipment free of accumulation of dust, dirt, food particles, and other debris.
